% js_builtins_nodes.dl — node half of the in-engine replacement for the
% Builtins.hs resolver (packages/grafema-resolve/src/Builtins.hs:282-357):
% EXTERNAL_MODULE + EXTERNAL_FUNCTION node minting for Node.js builtin modules.
% The EDGE half (IMPORTS_FROM / CALLS) lives in js_builtins_edges.dl — the
% engine-sanctioned two-pack split: a @materialize edge endpoint must be a
% node-ID column, and a node minted in the SAME run only has its id as the
% BLAKE3 of a rule-built string (the axum_routes.dl header limitation). The
% edges pack runs strictly AFTER this one (cross-pack EDB ordering contract).
%
% THE WAVE-1 VERDICT CORRECTIONS ARE LOAD-BEARING HERE (all three reproduced):
%   (a) the registry does NOT gate emission — resolveCallNode (Hs:317-339)
%       emits for ANY dotted call whose object is a builtin-imported local
%       name; lookupBuiltinFunc (Hs:326) only enriches security/pure metadata.
%       The three node heads below split on registry membership for the META
%       payload only; the non-registry head (ext_func_node_plain) keeps every
%       fs.openSync / fs.promises.readFile-class function that a
%       registry-gated rule would silently drop.
%   (b) the direct-call arm (Hs:353-357) is present: `import {join} from
%       'path'; join()` mints EXTERNAL_FUNCTION:path.join via the binding's
%       importedName (NOT its local name — aliased `import {join as j}` works).
%   (c) bare-name (module, name) disambiguation in the edges pack is
%       node_attr-dependent — therefore meta(module, …) is projected on EVERY
%       function head below, so the minted node carries `module` as a
%       top-level metadata field exactly where node_attr reads it
%       (http.get/https.get, path.parse/url.parse stay distinct).
%
% SEMANTIC IDS ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL to the legacy convention — REQUIRED for
% dedup against the still-ON legacy resolver (a present node is never
% rewritten; same sid ⇒ same BLAKE3 id ⇒ one node):
%   EXTERNAL_MODULE:<m>        (mkExternalModuleNode, Hs:364-376)
%   EXTERNAL_FUNCTION:<m>.<fn> (mkExternalFuncNode,  Hs:379-395)
% where <m> is the NORMALIZED module name ("node:fs" → "fs", Hs:57-61) and
% <fn> is the substring after the FIRST dot of the callee for method calls
% (T.breakOn ".", Hs:345 — e.g. "fs.promises.readFile" → m="fs",
% fn="promises.readFile") or the binding's importedName for direct calls.
% The first-dot split is reproduced by concat(LN, ".", P) + strip_prefix:
% binding local names never contain dots, so LN"." IS the first-dot prefix.
%
% NUMBERED DELTAS vs the resolver (everything not listed is exact):
%   DELTA 1 (metadata repr): `pure` is projected as the STRING "true"/"false"
%     (datalog values are strings); the legacy node carried a JSON bool
%     (MetaBool, Hs:393). While legacy mints first its node wins (present
%     nodes are never rewritten) — the delta is only visible once legacy is
%     gated. node_attr skips non-scalar values either way.
%   DELTA 2 (node surface): pack-minted nodes have no `exported` flag and no
%     line/column zeros (NodeRecordV2 has no such surface); legacy set
%     gnExported=True. Recorded loss — no known consumer reads exported on
%     EXTERNAL_* nodes.
%   DELTA 3 (superset, set semantics): the legacy import index was a Map with
%     last-wins on duplicate (file, localName) bindings (Hs:262-272); set
%     semantics derives per candidate. Duplicate bindings of one local name in
%     one file are near-nonexistent.
%   DELTA 4 (file gate): the resolver's effective gate was the orchestrator's
%     detect_language == JavaScript stream filter (8 extensions) — reproduced
%     as the 8-clause gates below on IMPORT and IMPORT_BINDING (cross-language
%     leakage guard: a Rust `use url::Url` binding or a non-JS IMPORT named
%     "os"/"crypto" must NOT mint Node-builtin externals). CALL nodes need no
%     own gate: every arm joins the call's file against a gated binding.
%   DELTA 5 (parity, deliberate): the legacy direct arm emits importedName
%     verbatim — `import fs from 'fs'; fs()` yields EXTERNAL_FUNCTION:fs.default
%     and a namespace `fs()` call yields EXTERNAL_FUNCTION:fs.* — both
%     reproduced (no guard), byte-parity over cosmetics.
%
% MAINTAIN ENVELOPE: node_attr + negation + node minting ⇒ scratch floor.
%
% ORDERING (PRODUCER): MUST run before js_builtins_edges (which joins these
% nodes as committed EDB) and therefore before method_calls / shape_verifier.
% mode = "exclusive" on the node heads is PROVENANCE-SCOPED (engine contract):
% only nodes stamped with THIS rule's _source are owned/retracted; the legacy
% resolver's identically-sid'd nodes are foreign and never touched.

% ── Generated ground facts: builtin module specifiers → normalized name ──
% (Builtins.hs:79-246 module set; "node:" twins per normalizeModuleName :57-61)
builtin_spec("fs", "fs").
builtin_spec("node:fs", "fs").
